# The build context for both server/Dockerfile and client/Dockerfile is the repo root (so a
# single Dockerfile can COPY sibling workspace package.json files) — Docker only ever reads a
# .dockerignore from the context root, so this one file governs both builds.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/*.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore

**/src/test

# Dev/editor cruft that shouldn't bloat the build context
.vscode
.idea
*.md
